>
  <p>
    <strong>Golden Moments is for recreation and general information only.</strong> Nothing on this website is medical
    advice, and nothing here replaces care from a doctor, nurse, pharmacist, registered dietitian or other qualified
    professional who knows the person.
  </p>
  <h2>Our games</h2>
  <p>
    Our games and activities are for enjoyment and shared time. They do not diagnose, test, measure, treat, slow or
    prevent dementia, Alzheimer’s disease or any other condition. Activities are not suitable for everyone. Follow the
    person’s interests and comfort, and stop or change an activity when needed.
  </p>
  <h2>Our health and research pages</h2>
  <p>
    Our brain health pages summarize published research for a general audience. Research findings describe groups of
    people and cannot tell you what will happen to one person. Talk with a doctor before changing diet, fasting, exercise,
    sleep habits, medicines or supplements, especially for an older adult or someone living with dementia.
  </p>
  <h2>When to get help right away</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Call <strong>911</strong> for an emergency, such as sudden confusion, trouble speaking, weakness on one side, a fall with injury or chest pain.</li>
    <li>Contact a doctor promptly for new or quickly worsening memory problems, confusion, agitation, refusing food or drink, or other sudden changes.</li>
    <li>The Alzheimer’s Association 24/7 Helpline is <strong>1-800-272-3900</strong>.</li>
    <li>If you are a caregiver in crisis, you can call or text <strong>988</strong>.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    We link to sources we trust, but we do not control other websites and are not responsible for their content.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
